  "status": "full normal-feature build passed; native requalification running before normal browser matrix",
  "recorded_at": "2026-10-28T01:04:47.844633+00:00",
  "motivation": {
    "runtime_witness": "docs/evidence/gate-6/browser-audio-post-fix-gaps.json",
    "observed": "Post-fix source and server Opus payloads decode cleanly, but output RTP has missing20ms intervals. Complete43616event server timeline has no omissions. Fresh ingress uses the controller model mutex across external policy reads; retained mixer acquisition intentionally refuses temporary model contention.",
    "scope_limit": "New component regression proves the avoidable mutex hold. Full normal runtime is required to determine how much it explains the captured audio/cadence/WT failures; no complete causal-repair claim from component tests."
  },
  "implementation": [
    "Fresh non-data publication snapshots original stream revision, credential, consumer and scene metadata before releasing controller model mutex for external policy admission. Snapshots own no positive policy grant or route/consumer/scene reader.",
    "After callback, reacquire metadata without waiting while holding authority, validate original revision/credential/active binding and require the original consumer/scene stamp. A new owner or a formerly absent owner cannot be silently adopted.",
    "Actual model mutex contention for fresh ingress is explicit Backpressure, allowing existing ingress retry owners to retain the same original packet. Retained metadata keeps existing NotReady behavior. Original age, audience authorization, codec queues and IO deadlines are unchanged. Reliable-data/held-control paths retain their existing protocol."
  ],
